      "type": "text",
      "x": -400,
      "y": 270,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "### Assistant\n- **S00.01-04-00** Talk Bot Service (RIO model)"
    },
    {
      "id": "tk-sharing",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -400,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "### Sharing\n- **S00.02-00-00** Storymap Sharing Model"
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-header",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": -300,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE\n**OS metaphor — layers from I/O down to storage**"
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-io",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": -210,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 100,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## I/O Adapters\nSame kernel, different mouths and ears\n\n| Adapter | Status |\n|---------|--------|\n| **CLI** (`servetus_cli.py`) | Active |\n| **Nextcloud Talk** (`nextcloud/talk.py`) | Scaffolded |\n| **Obsidian Plugin** | Planned |\n| **System Tray** | Planned |\n| **Voice (Shokz)** | Phase 4 |"
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-shell",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": -80,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## Shell\nInterprets commands via Toolkit specs"
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-kernel",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 10,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "## Kernel\n**AI processes instructions — same interpreter everywhere.**\nYou sit here. Not at the top. Not as the authority."
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-libs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## System Libs\nToolkit/ — the spec library"
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-userspace",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 420,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## User Space\nconfig/ — user settings (gitignored)"
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-fs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 190,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## File System\n00-system → 01-witnesses → 02-daily-logs → ... → 07-storymap"
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-storage",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 280,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## Storage + Sync (Trust-Tiered)\n\n| Tier | Destination | Clearance |\n|------|------------|----------|\n| **Sovereign** | Nextcloud / self-hosted | Everything |\n| **Controlled** | Private Git | Code + specs |\n| **Public** | Public Git | Standards only |\n| **Transient** | Ephemeral LLM | Processing only |"
    },
    {
      "id": "rio-header",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 800,
      "y": -300,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# RIO — PERSONAL ASSISTANT\n**You're the pilot. The assistant is your RIO.**"
    },
    {
      "id": "rio-model",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 800,
      "y": -210,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "0",
      "text": "## The RIO Model (F-14 Tomcat)\n\n- **Situational awareness** — calendar, projects, tasks, radar\n- **Covers blind spots** — ADD gaps in follow-through & context-switching\n- **Sits in meetings** — listening, extracting action items\n- **Post-call processing** — distributes info across PIM surface\n- **Context maintenance** — remembers what you need where\n- **Proactive not intrusive** — surfaces what's relevant, stays quiet in flow\n\n*\"Talk to me, Goose\"* → `brief.sitrep`"
    },
    {
      "id": "rio-runtime",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 800,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 140,
      "color": "0",
      "text": "## Bot Runtime (3 Layers)\n\n**1. Talk Client** — polls Talk room, sends responses\n(extends existing `TalkListener`)\n\n**2. Intent Parser** — local LLM turns natural language → structured Intent\n(action, service, target, confidence, sub-intents)\n\n**3. PIM Executor** — routes intents to Nextcloud services\n(WebDAV, CalDAV, CardDAV, REST APIs)"
    },
    {
      "id": "rio-pim",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 800,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "0",
      "text": "## Nextcloud PIM Surface\nThe assistant's hands — not just files\n\n| Service | Protocol | Ops |\n|---------|----------|-----|\n| Files | WebDAV | read, create, move, summarize |\n| Calendar | CalDAV | check, free, create, move, cancel |\n| Contacts | CardDAV | find, create, update, notes |\n| Tasks | VTODO | list, create, complete, defer |\n| Deck | REST | status, create, move, assign |\n| Notifications | REST | send reminders, check |\n\n**Cross-service:** morning brief, weekly preview, meeting prep, intake capture"
    },
    {
      "id": "rio-hardware",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 800,
      "y": 400,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "0",
      "text": "## Hardware Phases\n\n| Phase | Hardware | LLM |\n|-------|----------|-----|\n| **1 — Now** | Home PC, 1080 Ti (11GB) | Llama 3 8B Q4 via Ollama |\n| **2** | Mac Mini M1/M3, colocated | Llama 3 8B–70B via MLX |\n| **3** | Scaled fleet | Multiple Minis, multiple bots |\n| **4** | Voice-first | Shokz + Whisper + TTS |"
    },
    {
      "id": "voice-pipeline",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 140,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "## Voice Pipeline\n`00-system/voice/`\n\n**Capture** → Whisper STT → Prosody analysis → SVP format\n\nReused by:\n- Meeting mode (passive observation)\n- Phase 4 voice interface\n- Witness filing (audio → transcript)"
    },
    {
      "id": "nextcloud-adapters",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 480,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 140,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "## Nextcloud Adapters\n`00-system/nextcloud/`\n\n**Exists:**\n- talk.py, webdav.py, config.py, archive.py\n\n**Needed:**\n- caldav.py, carddav.py, deck.py, notify.py"
    },
    {
      "id": "bot-code",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 650,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "## Bot Service Code (To Build)\n`00-system/bot/`\n\n- `intent.py` — Intent parser (LLM-backed)\n- `executor.py` — PIM executor\n\n`00-system/bot-prompts/`\n- `copilot.md` — Primary assistant personality"
    },
    {
      "id": "cli-commands",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 480,
      "y": 650,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "## CLI Commands (To Build)\n\n```\nservetus bot start <name>\nservetus bot stop <name>\nservetus bot status\nservetus bot list\nservetus bot exec <name> \"msg\"\nservetus bot api <name> --port\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "principles",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -400,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "# Core Principles\n\n1. **You are not the authority.** Witnesses define what happened.\n2. **Everything is human-readable.** If software dies, the folder survives.\n3. **Submission, not collection.** Every artifact is intentional.\n4. **Consent is granular.** Each data source is separate opt-in.\n5. **Sovereignty over privacy.** Architecture, not policy.\n6. **Exclusion is valid.** Gaps are deliberate.\n7. **Deletion is real.** Gone means gone."
    },
    {
      "id": "status-now",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 800,
      "y": 600,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# STATUS — March 9, 2026\n\n**Specs:** 13 toolkit specs written\n**Code:** CLI + voice pipeline + Nextcloud adapters scaffolded\n**Docs:** Philosophy, CLAUDE.md, SETUP, CHANGELOG\n**Vault:** Folder structure live, altitude model applied\n\n**Next moves:**\n- Merge branch to `personal`\n- Build CalDAV/CardDAV clients\n- Build intent parser + PIM executor\n- Wire up `servetus bot start`\n- Phase 1 deployment on home PC with Ollama"
    }
  ],
